  <p class="exp-legend" data-both>
    <span data-zh>档位：<b>A</b> 全链 TTS —— 可出完整节目 ｜ <b>B</b> 真声/学者 —— 母语者口播，字幕后置 ｜ 其余候选池语暂走 <b>C</b> 词卡档。</span>
    <span data-en>Tiers: <b>A</b> full TTS chain (full episodes) ｜ <b>B</b> native-voice / scholar recordings, captions fall back ｜ candidates in reserve run as <b>C</b> word-cards.</span>
  </p>

  <div class="teach-note">
    <span data-zh><strong>新织线速览：</strong>复兴三姐妹 he · ga · mi（把语言说回来）／文字三命运 ar · fa · tr（保留-改造-决裂）／借词回旋镖 es ↔ nah（chocolate、tomato 出境）／包罗性 we·qu · tpi · id（「你们算不算我们」）／声调群 zh · th · vi · yo · yua／海词族 ar · sw · id · mi · tpi（印度洋到太平洋的帆影）。逐语身份卡与选语五原则见 </span>
    <span data-en><strong>New weaving threads:</strong> the revival sisters he · ga · mi; three fates of script ar · fa · tr; the loanword boomerang es ↔ nah (chocolate, tomato); the inclusive-we qu · tpi · id; the tone club zh · th · vi · yo · yua; the sea-faring family ar · sw · id · mi · tpi. Full identity cards and the five selection lenses live in the </span>
    <a href="../../Language%20Stacking-Linguistic%20Weaving/LANGUAGES_LINGUISTIC_EXPANSION.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span data-zh>32 语扩展蓝图</span><span data-en>32-Language Expansion Blueprint</span></a>
  </div>
</section><!-- ═══ PART B ═══ -->

<!-- ═══ GOJŪON ═══ -->
<section class="section band-paper" id="gojuon">
  <div class="section-header">
    <h2><span data-zh>日本語 · 五十音図</span><span data-en>Nihongo · Gojūon</span></h2>
    <div class="subtitle"><span data-zh>声音变成文字的第一步</span><span data-en>Where voice becomes script</span></div>
    <span class="divider"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="goji-intro" data-both>
    <span data-zh>五十音＝清音 46 音（5 段 × 9 行 + 撥音 ん）。行以辅音命名、段以元音命名（a i u e o）；し・ち・つ・ふ 保留古音拼写；を 与 お 同音、仅作助词；ん 为独立音节鼻音。浊音・半浊音・拗音・长音皆由此派生。</span>
    <span data-en>The gojūon is the 46 pure sounds: 5 vowel-columns × 9 consonant-rows, plus the syllabic nasal ん. Rows take their consonant, columns their vowel (a·i·u·e·o). し·ち·つ·ふ keep archaic spellings; を sounds like お and is only a particle; ん is a syllabic nasal. Voiced, semi-voiced, contracted and long sounds all derive from these.</span>
  </div>

  <div class="kana-wrap">
    <table class="kana-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>行 Row</th><th class="vowel">あ a</th><th class="vowel">い i</th><th class="vowel">う u</th><th class="vowel">え e</th><th class="vowel">お o</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="rowname">あ行</td>
          <td class="kana-cell"><span class="k">ア</span><span class="h">あ</span><span class="r">a</span></td>
          <td class="kana-cell"><span class="k">イ</span><span class="h">い</span><span class="r">i</span></td>
